{"availability":"available","full":"erichlof/THREE.js-PathTracing-Renderer","name":"THREE.js-PathTracing-Renderer","description":"Real-time PathTracing with global illumination and progressive rendering, all on top of the Three.js WebGL framework. Click here for Live Demo: https://erichlof.github.io/THREE.js-PathTracing-Renderer/Geometry_Showcase.html","category":"Developer tools","language":"GLSL","stars":2250,"forks":202,"created":"2016-07-12T06:24:51Z","updated":"2026-07-07T20:39:41Z","license":"CC0-1.0","branch":"gh-pages","homepage":"","topics":["global-illumination","path","path-tracer","pathtracing","ray","raytracing","realtime","three-js","threejs","tracer","tracing","webgl"],"demo":"https://erichlof.github.io/THREE.js-PathTracing-Renderer/Geometry_Showcase.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:29:02.235Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:29:02.235Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:29:02.235Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:12.636Z","stars":2251,"forks":202},{"at":"2026-10-07T23:29:02.235Z","stars":2250,"forks":202}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Real-time PathTracing with global illumination and progressive rendering, all on top of the Three.js WebGL framework.","Once I had Kevin's basic smallPT ported to JavaScript/WebGL and working in the browser, I started to add my own features little by little over the years, with the end goal being something that performs as well as the Brigade renderers, and looks as good as a final smallPT output rendering, but that works everywhere on any device (even tablets and cell phones!). So far, the features that I have added include: real-time progressive rendering on any device with a browser, FirstPerson Camera controls with Depth of Field, a more complete Ray-Object intersection support library (such as planes,…","More examples, features, and content to come!"],"features":["Real-time interactive Path Tracing at 30-60 FPS in your brow